# Naming & Imports

## Purpose

Consistent, greppable names across the codebase.

## When Applied

Any `lib/**/*.dart` edit that adds or renames files, types, or imports.

## Requirements

| Kind | Convention |
|------|------------|
| Files / folders | `snake_case` |
| Types | `PascalCase` |
| Members | `camelCase`; private `_underscore` |
| BLoC trio | `*_bloc.dart`, `*_event.dart`, `*_state.dart` |
| Repositories | `*_repository.dart` (auth: `*_repo.dart` / `AuthRepo`) |
| Models | `*_model.dart` |
| Datasources | `*_remote_ds.dart` |
| DB / JSON keys | `snake_case` matching Postgres |

- Match the type to the filename (`FooCubit` → `foo_cubit.dart`).
- Prefer consistency with the nearest sibling file in the same feature.

## Examples

- `sessions_repository.dart` exposes `SessionsRepository`.

## Anti-patterns

- New typos or odd casing (`catgeory_*`, `splach_*`, `Login_header.dart`).
- A second `*_page.dart` beside an existing one with a legacy-duplicate name.

## Common Mistakes

- Putting a Cubit inside a `*_bloc.dart` file.
- JSON keys in `camelCase` that no longer match the Postgres column.
